    "bio": "a Representative from New Jersey; born in Englewood, Bergen County, N.J., July 9, 1959; graduated from High Point Regional High School, Sussex, N.J., 1977; B.A., Montclair State University, Montclair, N.J., 1981; J.D., Rutgers University Law School, Camden, N.J., 1984; lawyer, private practice; member of the New Jersey state general assembly, 1990-2002; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Eighth and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2003-January 3, 2017); unsuccessful candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Fifteenth Congress in 2016; staff, United States Securities and Exchange Commission, 2018-2021.",
